# TypeScript Standards

## Type Definitions
```typescript
// ✅ Export interfaces from types/index.ts
export interface Company {
  id: string
  _id?: string  // MongoDB ID
  name: string
  status: CompanyStatus
}

// ✅ Use type for unions/aliases
export type CompanyStatus = 'pending' | 'active' | 'inactive' | 'archived'

// ✅ Form data types
export interface CreateCompanyFormData {
  name: string
  email: string
}

export interface UpdateCompanyFormData {
  name?: string  // Optional for partial updates
  email?: string
}
```

## Naming Conventions
- Interfaces: `PascalCase` (e.g., `Company`, `UserProfile`)
- Types: `PascalCase` (e.g., `CompanyStatus`)
- Functions: `camelCase` (e.g., `fetchCompanies`)
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` (e.g., `COUNTRIES`)
- Files: `kebab-case.ts` (e.g., `company-management.tsx`)

## Error Handling
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Typed error handling
try {
  const result = await apiCall()
  if (!result.success) {
    throw new Error(result.error)
  }
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Operation failed:', error)
  toast({ title: t('error'), variant: 'destructive' })
}
```

## Avoid
- `any` type - use `unknown` and narrow
- Non-null assertions `!` - use optional chaining
- Implicit returns in complex functions
